{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1253, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nGiven an array of integers nums and an integer k, an element nums[i] is considered good if it is strictly greater than the elements at indices i - k and i + k (if those indices exist). If neither of these indices exists, nums[i] is still considered good.\nReturn the sum of all the good elements in the array.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [1,3,2,1,5,4], k = 2\nOutput: 12\nExplanation:\nThe good numbers are nums[1] = 3, nums[4] = 5, and nums[5] = 4 because they are strictly greater than the numbers at indices i - k and i + k.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [2,1], k = 1\nOutput: 2\nExplanation:\nThe only good number is nums[0] = 2 because it is strictly greater than nums[1].\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n2 <= nums.length <= 100\n1 <= nums[i] <= 1000\n1 <= k <= floor(nums.length / 2)\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def sumOfGoodNumbers(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> int:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1303, "char_start": 1265, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 3, 2, 1, 5, 4]\n2\nOutput:\n12", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1340, "char_start": 1315, "quote": "Input:\n[2, 1]\n1\nOutput:\n2", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "9c3737edc6bdec192a69ce00a65df3aae3f901ac753f68afa35809d84324f1e3", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "0d2f7ac4c573a50fd16e661c125b452899fedfe2de9697739428b0c89214b490", "seq": 2}
